    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d912">

                <pb facs="0851" n="843" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg843"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102 Tientsin/559: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Tientsin</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tientsin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-01-27T12:00:00+08:00">January 27,
                        1940—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 5:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>11. My telegram No. 9, January 24, 4 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d912-f1"/> I have
                    been notified informally by the Japanese Consulate General that from tomorrow
                        <pb facs="0852" n="844" xml:id="pg844"/> electrified fence around British
                    and French Concessions will again be charged. Evidently it has not been charged
                    since submerged by August flood.</p>
                <p>So far as reported, expiration of treaty<anchor n="2" xml:id="d912-f2"/> has not
                    brought noticeable change in the attitude of the Japanese military toward
                    Americans that could safely be ascribed to that cause, though there may be less
                    cordiality on the part of some sentries than formerly. Increased barrier
                    difficulties appear to affect other nationals as well and in some cases may be
                    due to changes in personnel at barriers.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Peiping, Shanghai, air mail to Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caldwell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
